            <ArticleTitle>Is the prevalence of severe stenoses of left circumflex different from that of the right coronary artery?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>114-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We reviewed the last 911 coronary arteriograms performed in our laboratory because of chest pain. Among 215 patients with single-vessel disease, 40 had stenosis in the right coronary artery and 43 in the left circumflex. This finding conflicts with previous reports. Perhaps racial differences could explain this discrepancy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
